From: pzl8-nss project
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: ipq5018: widen the Q6/WCSS reserved region

ath11k hands the firmware raw physical addresses for the board data and the
m3 dump (qcom,bdf-addr / qcom,m3-dump-addr). On PZ-L8 those are 0x4c400000
for the built-in radio and 0x4d100000 / 0x4df00000 for the QCN6122, but
wcss@4b000000 only spans 0x4b000000-0x4cb00000, so the QCN6122 addresses are
outside any reserved region and the built-in radio gets 7 MiB where the
firmware wants 13 MiB. Both radios then fail BDF download with -ENOMEM:

    ath11k c000000.wifi: failed to load board data file: -12
    ath11k b00a040.wifi: failed to load board data file: -12

The vendor firmware for this exact board (nwrt, kernel 5.4) reserves
0x4b000000-0x4f100000 as q6_mem_regions, with q6_ipq5018_data at 0x4c400000
(13 MiB), m3_dump at 0x4d100000 and the QCN6122 data regions above that.
Match that span so both radios have their windows.

Costs ~38 MiB of system RAM, which is why upstream disabled the radios here
instead; 0818 gives 8 MiB of that back by trimming the NSS region to the size
the vendor firmware actually uses.

Signed-off-by: pzl8-nss
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
@@ -161,7 +161,7 @@
 		};
 
 		q6_region: wcss@4b000000 {
-			reg = <0x0 0x4b000000 0x0 0x1b00000>;
+			reg = <0x0 0x4b000000 0x0 0x4100000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
 	};
